      "textEn": "228\nThe driver sits in it and drives it according to his will. This is also confirmed in the Bhagavad Gita (18.61)--Jiva, as if mounted on a body-like machine, and the body-like motorcar, remaining under the control of nature,\nmoves and walks, just as trains move by staying in the path-guidance of the controller. But these beings are not bodies; they are separate from the body-like vehicle. But the ignorant material\nscientist does not know the method of joining the parts of the body, which are in the form of senses, mind, and qualities. Every living being is a spiritual spark, a part of the Supreme Being, and just as a father is merciful to his son,\nin the same way, by the grace of God, every living being has been given a little independence so that they may freely act by asserting dominion over the qualities of nature.\nJust as a father, while crying, hands over toys to quiet a child, similarly, by the will of God, to allow the deluded beings to exercise their dominion over their desired objects under the control of God's representative,\nthe entire material creation\nis made. All beings are playing in the physical playground like those small children whose\nsupervision is being done by the maidservant (Prakriti) of God. They, considering this maidservant or illusion as the supreme,\nconsider the absolute truth as Khri (FRE etc.). Foolish, child-like materialistic slaves of nature\nare not able to rise above the concept, but the intelligent and wise sons of God know very well that\nall the works of nature are controlled by God in the same way as the father-like of unadvanced children\nremains subject to their master.\nThe body's parts, such as the senses, are created by the great element, and when these parts, by the will of God, become one,\n\nthen the physical body comes into existence, and the living being is allowed to use it for its future tasks. Its explanation is given further. Then, being endowed with the power of the Lord, they are united in the three qualities.\n\nHaving obtained good and bad, they are united in the three qualities. 33. Meaning of the word:\n\nTada--Then; Sab-All; Sam-Together; Cha--Also; Anyon-Each other; Bhagavat-By God; Shakti-Power;\nChodita-Used; Sat-Truth; Asat-Untruth; Upaday-Accepting; Cha--Also; Ubhayam-Both;\nSasujah-Uttayna Haa; Hi-Indeed; Adah-This world."
