      "textEn": "230\nYears-ago--many years; thousands-of-thousands-of-years; Tatu--that; Andamu--universe; Udake--in water; Shayam--\nDrowned; Kaal--eternal time; Karma--action; Swabhav-sthah--by nature's qualities; Jiva--lord of living beings; Ajivam--\nInanimate; Ajivayat--lived.. All\nThe lord of all beings entered into them and made them fully alive. Meaning: Here, God is called a living being, because he is the leader of all other living beings. In the Vedas,\nHe is called eternal, the leader of all eternals. The relationship of God with living beings is just like that\nJust like a father with his sons. In terms of quality, a son and a father are equal, but the father is neither a son, nor is the father the one who creates a son.\nIn this way, as has been said above,\nGarbhodakshayi Vishnu or Hiranyagarbha Paramatma enter every universe and from the womb of nature,\nthey create living beings and make them alive, as is confirmed in Bhagavad Gita (14.3). Physical\nAfter every cycle of creation, all living beings merge into the body of God, and at the end of creation,\nthey are again conceived in the form of physical energy. Therefore, in the physical world, only physical power is the mother of living beings,\nand God appears to be their father. However, when life is given, all\nliving beings, being subject to time and power, start doing their natural work again, and in this way,\nvarious types of living beings appear. Therefore, God is the reason for making this world alive.\nIs. He who is of the nature of a man, is free from the duality.\nSahasrarvadhida- Bahakshah sahasranan- Shirshavan. 25. Meaning of the word:\n\nSaha-- He (God); Eva-- Exactly; Purusha-- God; Tasmāt-- From within the universe; Andam-- Golden womb; Nirbhidya-- Without auspiciousness;\nNirgatah-- Having come out; Sahasrah-- Thousands; Oru-Je; Adri-Paṇa; Bahu-Bhujaḥ; Akshah-Aṅkhaḥ;\nSahasrah-- Thousands; Aṇan-Mouth; Shirshāvanu-With head..\n\nAlthough Lord (Mahavishnu) keeps sleeping in Karanarav, but he, coming out of it,\nHaving divided himself into the form of Hiranyagarbha, entered each universe,\nAnd he assumed a huge form with thousands - thousands of feet, arms, mouth, and head."
