      "textEn": "233\nHe can help by serving other higher classes and can benefit from their cooperation.\nCan. Therefore, this universe is a complete unit in the context of God. In the absence of this\nrelationship with God, the entire human society remains disordered, there is no peace and prosperity in it.\nThis is confirmed in the Vedas-- Trayamnosya mukhamasid bahurajanyah kritah. The earth is imagined, the heavens are below, and the earth is above.\nThe heart is the self, the sky is the self, and the great world is the self. 38. Meaning of the word:\nBhoo- up to the netherworld; Lokah- worlds; Kalpitah- imagined or said; Padbhyamu- from the feet;\nBhuvaah- upper; Lokah- worlds; Asya- His (God's) ; Nabhitah- from the navel; Hada- from the heart; Swarlokah- the abode of the gods; Urasa- from the chest; Maharlokah- the abode of sages and saints; Maha-atmanah- of the Supreme Soul.\n.\nUp to the earth, all the lower realms are situated in their feet. The earth, the intermediate realms, and the middle realms are their\nlocated in the navel, and even higher realms than these, which are inhabited by gods and cultured sages - monks,\nare situated in the chest of God. Meaning: Within this universe, there are fourteen realms. The underworld is called Bhur Loka, the middle\nBhu Loka, and the supreme realm up to the universe is called Brahmaloka. Up to there, all the upper realms are called Swarloka\nare called. All these worlds are situated in the body of the Lord. In other words, within this universe, there is no\nsuch world that is not related to God. The worlds of the Grihya are his, the world of the forest is the world of penance, from the breasts is born.\nThe head is the world of truth, the world of Brahma is eternal. 39). Meaning of the word:\nGreevyam-- up to the neck; Janaloka-- Janaloka; Asya-- his; Tapoloka-- Tapoloka; Stana-drayat-- starting from the chest;\nMurdhabhishah-- from the head; Satyaloka-- Satyaloka; Tu-- but; Brahmaloka-- the spiritual world; Sanat