      "textEn": "235\nSrila Sridhar Swami rightly says that the Brahmaloka Vaikuntha mentioned here is eternal,\nTherefore, it is not like the previously described physical creations. The immense form of God is the imagination of the material world. It has nothing to do with the spiritual world or the abode of God. The immediate, the hidden, the unseen, the all-pervading.\n\nThe pure, the son of the Janbhas, the unseen, the all-pervading. 40>. Mahatla tu gulphabhyam pradapabhyam rasatalam. The earth is the foot-tip of the netherworld, and the world is the man. 41). Meaning of the word:\nTat--His; Katyam--In the waist; Cha--Also; Atalam--Under the earth, the first realm; Krruptam--Possessed; Urubhyam--In the thighs;\nVitalam--The second realm below; Vibhooh--Of the Lord; Janubhyam--In the knees; Sutalam--The third realm below; Shuddham--Pure;\nJakghabhyam--In the joint; Tu--But; Talatalam--The fourth realm below; Mahatalam--The fifth realm below; Tu--\nBut; Gulphabhyam--of the ankle or the heel; Prapadbhyam--of the upper or front part of the foot; Rasatalam--the sixth chakra below; Padatlal--in the soles of the feet; Iti--thus; Lokamayah--pervaded by the worlds; Puman--man..\nOh son Narad, you should know from me that out of the fourteen realms, seven are the netherworlds. Among these, the first\nrealm is Atal, which is located in the waist, the second realm is Vital, located in the thighs, the third realm is Sutal\nin the knees, the fourth realm is Talatal in the calves, the fifth realm is Mahatal in the ankles, the sixth realm\nis Rasatal, which is located in the upper part of the feet, and the seventh realm is Patal Lok, which is located in the soles\nof the feet. Thus, the cosmic form of God is complete with all the worlds.\nMeaning: Modern adventurers (space travelers) can obtain this information from Shrimad Bhagwat,\n\nthat there are fourteen realms in space. Their position is considered from the Earth realm, which is\ncalled Bhur Lok. Above Bhur Lok is Bhuvar